      "writtenOn": "2021-12-07T16:36:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The typical pattern is you need to create a bool Kconfig and an int Kconfig.  The reason is the int Kconfig is always defined, so cannot be used in the #ifdef check.\n\ne.g.\n\nconfig PLATFORM_EC_XXX_OVERRIDE\n    bool \"Override xxx power-on default\"\n    help\n        Override the power-on default for XXX parameter. \n    \nif PLATFORM_EC_XXX_OVERRIDE\nconfig PLATFORM_EC_XXX\n    int \"Value to use for xxx override\"\n    range 0-3\n    help\n        Valid override values are 0 (1.25 A), 1 (1.75 A), etc.\nendif\n        \nYou could organize PLATFORM_EC_XXX as a choice, but that seems like overkill.  This setting should ultimately move into the devicetree.",
      "parentUuid": "e540d027_d3889092",
      "revId": "35bfc9d702c5e74b4f1cb73de48041b49a8cccbc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a4a2554_fb9c473c",
        "filename": "zephyr/Kconfig.usbc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 904,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-07T21:19:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As it happens, both of these configs are defined to a default value in config.h. I don\u0027t see any code that checks them with #ifdef, and I don\u0027t see any boards that leave them undefined. The code seems to assume that they will be defined.\n\nThat being the case, are you OK with leaving out a bool guard config item until this information makes its way into the device tree?",
      "parentUuid": "79ab6950_760c29fa",
      "revId": "35bfc9d702c5e74b4f1cb73de48041b49a8cccbc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
